      "document_hash": "0aa23a90c98867084c5a2999aa568669880a914d48bc48c474272f1ca62c3172",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0aa23a90c988-0000-0001",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES: SETH P. WAXMAN, ESQUIRE, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Petitioner. PAUL D. CLEMENT, ESQUIRE, Alexandria, Virginia; on behalf of the Respondent in support of the Petitioner. CHRISTOPHER G. MICHEL, ESQUIRE, Washington, D.C.; Court-appointed amicus curiae in support of the judgment below."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Richard Eugene Glossip)",
      "case_id": "scotus-22-7466",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0aa23a90c98867084c5a2999aa568669880a914d48bc48c474272f1ca62c3172",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0aa23a90c988-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There is no adequate or independent jurisdictional bar to review and no warrant for an evidentiary hearing. As to independence, the court's opinion is suffused with merits determinations on the Brady and Napue claims. And, certainly, there is no \"clear and express statement\" that the court's decision is based on a bona fide separate, adequate, and independent grounds, as long required by this Court to preclude review."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "scotus-22-7466",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0aa23a90c98867084c5a2999aa568669880a914d48bc48c474272f1ca62c3172",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0aa23a90c988-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Mr. Waxman, you place quite a bit of weight on the note --notes from Smothermon and Ackley, and from your opening statement, you clearly do not agree with them. Did you at any point get a statement from either one of the prosecutors?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "scotus-22-7466",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0aa23a90c98867084c5a2999aa568669880a914d48bc48c474272f1ca62c3172",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0aa23a90c988-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: And everything that the Oklahoma courts have done, you said a hundred years of their history, party presentation, the fact that they've never had a case with a constitutional violation where they didn't accept the waiver, correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Paul D. Clement",
      "case_id": "scotus-22-7466",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0aa23a90c98867084c5a2999aa568669880a914d48bc48c474272f1ca62c3172",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0aa23a90c988-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "conclusion that Brady and Napue violations by the State's own prosecutors obligated him to confess error and waive procedural obstacles, as his predecessor had done in McCarty."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "scotus-22-7466",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0aa23a90c98867084c5a2999aa568669880a914d48bc48c474272f1ca62c3172",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0aa23a90c988-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Well -- well, shouldn't these two prosecutors -- it seems as though their reputations are being impugned, and, according to them, they did not receive an opportunity to explain in depth."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "scotus-22-7466",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0aa23a90c98867084c5a2999aa568669880a914d48bc48c474272f1ca62c3172",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0aa23a90c988-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What -- what do you take that to mean?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "scotus-22-7466",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0aa23a90c98867084c5a2999aa568669880a914d48bc48c474272f1ca62c3172",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0aa23a90c988-0002-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the State has only come forward with Napue arguments and Brady arguments"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "scotus-22-7466",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0aa23a90c98867084c5a2999aa568669880a914d48bc48c474272f1ca62c3172",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0aa23a90c988-0002-0003",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the State's concession is not based in law or fact."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "scotus-22-7466",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0aa23a90c98867084c5a2999aa568669880a914d48bc48c474272f1ca62c3172",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0aa23a90c988-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 80,
        "start": 80
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: What do we do with the other violations that the prosecutor committed?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "scotus-22-7466",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0aa23a90c98867084c5a2999aa568669880a914d48bc48c474272f1ca62c3172",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0aa23a90c988-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 86,
        "start": 86
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE JACKSON: Are you saying that statute is a jurisdictional one?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "scotus-22-7466",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0aa23a90c98867084c5a2999aa568669880a914d48bc48c474272f1ca62c3172",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0aa23a90c988-0004-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 92,
        "start": 92
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Can I ask you about the independence prong?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "scotus-22-7466",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0aa23a90c98867084c5a2999aa568669880a914d48bc48c474272f1ca62c3172",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0aa23a90c988-0005-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 110,
        "start": 110
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE JACKSON: -- whether there was a Brady or Napue violation here?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Michel",
      "case_id": "scotus-22-7466",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0aa23a90c98867084c5a2999aa568669880a914d48bc48c474272f1ca62c3172",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0aa23a90c988-0005-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 114,
        "start": 114
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Michel, this Court appointed you to brief and argue this case as an amicus curiae in support of the judgment below."
    },
